"Eeva","key":"berglundpedh","last":"Berglund","name":"Berglund, Eeva","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Guy","key":"julierpedh","last":"Julier","name":"Julier, Guy","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Per","key":"lindepedh","last":"Linde","name":"Linde, Per","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"59-67","publisher":"Syddansk Universitet","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of Nordes 2021: Matters of Scale. 15-18 August 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cbad3452-bf22-4a26-9d04-f5c29b0b0ad5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Envisioning Large-Scale Effects of Teaching Values in Design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-245715","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Spinocerebellar ataxia type 8 (SCA8), a dominantly inherited neurodegenerative disorder caused by a CTG•CAG expansion, is unusual because most individuals that carry the mutation do not develop ataxia. To understand the variable penetrance of SCA8, we studied the molecular differences between highly penetrant families and more common sporadic cases (82%) using a large cohort of SCA8 families (n = 77). We show that repeat expansion mutations from individuals with multiple affected family members have CCG•CGG interruptions at a higher frequency than sporadic SCA8 cases and that the number of CCG•CGG interruptions correlates with age at onset. At the molecular level, CCG•CGG interruptions increase RNA hairpin stability, and in cell culture experiments, increase p-eIF2α and polyAla and polySer RAN protein levels. Additionally, CCG•CGG interruptions, which encode arginine interruptions in the polyGln frame, increase toxicity of the resulting proteins. In summary, SCA8 CCG•CGG interruptions increase polyAla and polySer RAN protein levels, polyGln protein toxicity, and disease penetrance and provide novel insight into the molecular differences between SCA8 families with high vs. low disease penetrance.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Perez, Barbara A","Shorrock, Hannah K","Banez-Coronel, Monica","Zu, Tao","Romano, Lisa El","Laboissonniere, Lauren A","Reid, Tammy","Ikeda, Yoshio","Reddy, Kaalak","Gomez, Christopher M","Bird, Thomas","Ashizawa, Tetsuo","Schut, Lawrence J","Brusco, Alfredo","Berglund, J Andrew","Hasholt, Lis","Nielsen, Jørgen Erik","Subramony, S H","Ranum, Laura Pw"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-476510"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","Japan","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Gunma University","The Methodist Hospital Research Institute, Houston","The University of Chicago","University at Albany-SUNY","University of Florida","University of Minnesota Twin Cities","University of Turin"],"keyword":["Ataxia","Humans","Nerve Tissue Proteins genetics","Penetrance","Proteins","RNA Long Noncoding genetics","Trinucleotide Repeat Expansion"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Geology Department; Western Washington University; Bellingham Washington USA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ccg cgg interruptions in high penetrance sca000000000008 families increase ran translation and protein toxicity","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.15252/emmm.202114095","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-476510","identifier":[{"id":"85116739014","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8573593","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34632710","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-8af2876f-7e10-4feb-bd4e-860929a70dc7"],"keyword":["Ataxia","Humans","Nerve Tissue Proteins/genetics","Penetrance","Proteins","RNA, Long Noncoding/genetics","Spinocerebellar Degenerations/genetics","Trinucleotide Repeat Expansion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0E689BC84A4B13B7B303B572390EF064"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/298183333/EMBO_Mol_Med_2021_Perez_CCG_CGG_interruptions_in_high_u2010penetrance_SCA8_families_increase_RAN_translation_and_protein.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.15252/emmm.202114095","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of florida","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Universit