{"abstract":"In interrogations of scale and in questioning how things hang together, we have to maintain the insight that things, people and spaces can hang together in many ways. Multiple orders are at play in the world. Thinking and writing in topological ways – exploring approaches for laying out spaces and how to move with and across them – is helpful when we want to make sense of multiplicity and to find ways to move within and across manifold orders and the complex interconnections between them. Taking inspiration from topologically inspired spatialities and a recasting of the relationship between world, knowledge and performance, this conference paper explores fluid and dynamic models of knowing in and with a complex world. These models are related to education and design.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Svabo, Connie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-573367"],"event":{"end":"2021-08-18","place":"Kolding, dk","start":"2021-08-15","title":"NORDIC DESIGN RESEARCH CONFERENCE (NORDES)","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Svabo, Connie"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"living world dynamics or what brian eno can teach us about knowing in a complex world","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://conference2021nordes.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/final_Nordes-2021-Proceeding_jan22.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-573367","ids":["sdu-006225dc-ef83-4568-a25e-11a29ca140e7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AB86632ADBD93264D12147C7F3742F56"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Learning, Experience, and Design (LxD)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Connie","key":"svabopau","last":"Svabo","locid":"a72b95b2-fd34-4bca-8f09-3f9054c3f4e7","name":"Svabo, Connie","orcid":"0000-0001-5653-9222","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eva","key":"brandtpedh","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Eva","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"markussenpedh","last":"Markussen","name":"Markussen, Thomas","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Eeva","key":"berglundpedh","last":"Berglund","name":"Berglund, Eeva","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Guy","key":"julierpedh","last":"Julier","name":"Julier, Guy","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Per","key":"lindepedh","last":"Linde","name":"Linde, Per","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/nordes.2021.42","eisbn":["16049705"],"pages":"384-389","status":"p","subtitle":"Matters of Scale","title":"Proceedings of Nordes 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-006225dc-ef83-4568-a25e-11a29ca140e7"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Living World Dynamics : Or: what Brian Eno can teach us about knowing in a complex world","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-573367","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Data physicalization has emerged on the design scene as a way of making sense of big (quantitative) data. This study explores how bigdata physicalizations are designed, how people engage with them, and how that spurs innovation. Graduate student designers created 15 data physicalizations to engage bus planners and bus passengers at multi-stakeholder workshops in discussing bus services and bus designs. The physicalizations were based on passenger data from 9 city bus routes. We used dimensional analysis to scrutinize the data physicalizations as constructs and multimodal interaction analysis to understand how workshop participant interact with the physicalizations. Using the theories of Flow State and Play Moods as analytic perspectives we identified patterns of engagement that were stimulated by both material aspects of the data physicalizations and the designers’ role in facilitating interaction. We contribute with a framework of how data physicalizations can scale big data insights to meaningful engagements, which in turn lead to Small Beginnings of innovation","author_count":8,"contributors":["Buur, Jacob","Sorenson, Jessica","Cooper, Christina Melanie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-611719"],"event":{"acronym":"Nordes","end":"2021-08-18","place":"Kolding, dk","start":"2021-08-15","title":"NORDIC DESIGN RESEARCH CONFERENCE (NORDES)","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Buur, Jacob"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"big data and small beginnings how people engage with data physicalizations","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/nordes.2021.27","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-611719","ids":["sdu-866875c1-57ff-4d46-ae44-f72fd0397a64"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-68D40334F12593FFCFA38B156738BFC0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/nordes.2021.27","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/190687669/Big_data_small_beginnings_lo.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"buurpau","last":"Buur","locid":"c6a97ac7-3313-470b-b896-9958e843f962","name":"Buur, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-3320-1031","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jessica","key":"sorensonpau","last":"Sorenson","locid":"8947d277-d20c-4d6d-a649-188390313370","name":"Sorenson, Jessica","orcid":"0000-0002-7402-2347","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Melanie","key":"cooperpau","last":"Cooper","locid":"de8ff30d-acf7-4267-b537-809c816cf6d8","name":"Cooper, Christina Melanie","orcid":"0009-0007-5096-0658","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eva","key":"brandtpedh","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Eva","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"markussenpedh","last":"Markussen","name":"Markussen, Thomas","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Eeva","key":"berglundpedh","last":"Berglund","name":"Berglund, Eeva","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Guy","key":"julierpedh","last":"Julier","name":"Julier, Guy","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Per","key":"lindepedh","last":"Linde","name":"Linde, Per","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/nordes.2021.27","issn":["16049705"],"issue":"9","pages":"249-258","publisher":"Design School Kolding","series":"Nordic Design Research","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 9th Nordic Design Research Conference","title":"Nordes 2021: Matters of Scale"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-866875c1-57ff-4d46-ae44-f72fd0397a64"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Big data and small beginnings : how people engage with data physicalizations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-611719","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper reflects on experiences with practicing and scaling a social innovation concept that was co-produced between public and private partners and citizens in a living design laboratory in Denmark from 2009-2012. The concept is a public service supporting ad-hoc exercise communities for senior citizens in public parks, based on playful activities. This paper builds upon follow-up studies which have been made since the project ended. We discuss how practicing the service unfolded over time, and how two municipalities have attempted scaling the concept. We deepen the understanding of theoretical concepts of scaling with experiences from practice by e.g., discussing ownership, exchanges between formal institutions and informal civic engagement, and a need for clarifying new roles and responsibilities.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Yndigegn, Signe Louise","Malmborg, Lone","Foverskov, Maria","Brandt, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-736596"],"event":{"end":"2021-08-18","place":"Kolding, dk","start":"2021-08-15","title":"Nordes 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Malmö University, School of Arts and Communication (K3)"],"keyword":["Civic engagement","Ownership","Social innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-DSKD"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-DSKD","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"beyond a living lab scaling social innovation","src":["arkk"],"src-code":["DI-ART-DSKD"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/nordes.2021.36","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-736596","ids":["arkk-603d159b-2c8b-45af